# {{projectName}}

This pnpm workspace holds frontend apps and the packages they share.

**Coding agents:** Start with [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) for workspace rules and
verification, then use the [documentation index](docs/README.md) to find the
guide for your task.

## Setup

Use a supported Node.js version and the pinned pnpm version in
[package.json](package.json). CI uses the Node.js version in
[.node-version](.node-version).

### Run the default app

If the workspace has an app, run these commands from the repository root:

```sh
pnpm bootstrap
pnpm dev
```

`pnpm bootstrap` installs dependencies from the lockfile and prepares app
resources, including any local overrides. Open the URL printed by `pnpm dev`.
To run a different app, find its ID with `pnpm apps:list` and pass it to
`pnpm dev` using `--app`.

### Set up a bare workspace

If you generated the workspace without an app, install and build its shared
packages from the repository root:

```sh
pnpm install --frozen-lockfile
pnpm build:packages
```

The [app addition guide](docs/commands.md#add-apps-and-dependencies) explains how
to add an app from the template source checkout.

## Build and verify

Run `pnpm build --all` to build the apps, or run `pnpm validate` for workspace
checks, tests, and builds.

## Own the project

- Each app's README shows where to edit pages, resources, and configuration, and
  how to remove its examples. Its `src/site` holds editable starter declarations
  and `src/infra` holds the mechanisms they configure.
- After changing resource inputs, run `pnpm app:prepare --all` at the root.
- `packages/shared` holds reusable capabilities. `packages/site` and
  `packages/adapters` hold optional domain and service integrations.

See the [command reference](docs/commands.md) for app selection and resource
preparation, and the [architecture guide](docs/architecture.md) for ownership.
The [code standards](docs/code-standards.md) and
[monorepo standards](docs/monorepo-standards.md) cover changes to code and packages.
